Emerging Market Opportunities
Atomic Layer Etching
Atomic layer etching enables highly controlled material removal through cyclic surface-modification processes. Its potential for sub-nanometer precision creates opportunities in advanced logic and memory manufacturing, particularly where conventional plasma processes face increasingly narrow process windows.

Cryogenic and High-Aspect-Ratio Etching
The continued development of 3D NAND and advanced DRAM is creating demand for technologies that improve deep-feature etching, profile control, and selectivity. Cryogenic processes and specialized chamber designs offer opportunities for equipment suppliers serving advanced memory applications.

AI-Assisted Process Optimization
Etch systems generate extensive process and sensor data. Integrating advanced analytics and AI-based recipe control can help manufacturers improve chamber utilization, detect process variations, and support predictive maintenance. These capabilities may strengthen equipment suppliers' long-term relationships with semiconductor fabs.

